{
  "chapter": "durable-execution/why-durable-execution",
  "tier": "drill",
  "notes": [
    "The whole mechanism: effects go through the runtime, which appends each completed",
    "result to a journal. On recovery the function re-runs from the first line, and every",
    "step already in the journal returns its recorded result instead of executing.",
    "The journal is positional, because replay compares the sequence of effects rather",
    "than their values. A step that does not match the recording at its position is a",
    "non-determinism error: the runtime can no longer tell where in the code this",
    "execution is.",
    "crashAfter scripts how many new effects complete before the process dies. A crashed",
    "run returns nothing and keeps everything it journalled."
  ],
  "program": [
    { "name": "get_order", "result": "order-4921" },
    { "name": "compute_credit", "result": 420000 },
    { "name": "issue_credit", "result": "cr_8823_1" },
    { "name": "send_reply", "result": "sent" }
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "a-first-run-executes-every-step",
      "journal": [],
      "crashAfter": 4,
      "result": {
        "status": "completed",
        "results": ["order-4921", 420000, "cr_8823_1", "sent"],
        "executed": ["get_order", "compute_credit", "issue_credit", "send_reply"],
        "journal": [
          { "name": "get_order", "result": "order-4921" },
          { "name": "compute_credit", "result": 420000 },
          { "name": "issue_credit", "result": "cr_8823_1" },
          { "name": "send_reply", "result": "sent" }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a-crash-keeps-the-effects-that-completed",
